/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  membrane20_dspmde_pore_finite_difference  --  the charged pore SOLVED.

  THREE NF270 elements, two salts -- every unit has the SAME membrane
  (NF270_dspmde: r_p 0.6 nm, X_d = -5 mol/m3, Born on), the same 10 bar, the
  same 5 mM feed of its salt:

       NF_NaCl_pore           transport DSPM-DE;  transportParameters {
       NF_MgSO4_pore            poreSolver { method finiteDifference;
                                             nodes 101; } }
       NF_MgSO4_closedForm    transport DSPM-DE;  transportParameters {
                                poreSolver { method closedForm; } }

  The `_pore` units DECLARE what has been DSPM-DE's default since
  2026-10-24 (DEV.md 4c C141) -- the pore solved on 101 nodes, the wall
  closed with that pore's own permeate (`wallClosure porePermeate`, the
  default too) -- so the declaration is visible; membrane10 and membrane11
  run the same model with nothing declared.

  WHAT `finiteDifference` SOLVES.  The extended Nernst-Planck equation of
  every ion on 101 nodes across the pore, electroneutrality with the fixed
  charge at EVERY node, zero net current, and the Donnan + steric + Born
  partitions at both faces -- every node at once, by Newton on the declared
  block-tridiagonal structure; and the wall (the multi-ionic film) closed
  with the permeate that pore gives, the two converged together.  That is
  the method of NanoFiltran (Geraldes & Alves, "Computer program for
  simulation of mass transport in nanofiltration membranes", J. Membr.
  Sci. 321 (2008) 172-182): the problem is STIFF -- a co-ion held back by
  the Donnan field carries a migration and a diffusion flux far larger than
  the flux they net, and the run prints that ratio ("stiffness") beside its
  residuals.

  WHAT THE CLOSED FORM DOES NOT SOLVE, and why only ONE unit carries it.
  `method closedForm;` (the default until 2026-10-24) makes the pore
  electroneutral at the FEED face, the permeate electroneutral, and carries
  each ion across ALONE by a closed-form transmission -- no potential
  gradient couples the ions inside the pore, and neither electroneutrality
  nor zero current is imposed there; its wall is closed with the salt's
  solution-diffusion B_s.  With the corrected hindrance (K_d = H/Phi, DEV.md
  4c C141) its transmission tends to K_c > 1 at low Peclet number, so on
  this membrane it returns a NaCl permeate RICHER than the wall: the bulk is
  exhausted inside the channel and the module refuses the run (its solute
  balance does not close).  This case used to carry an NF_NaCl_closedForm
  unit; it was removed for that reason, and bin/curate/check_pore_solver.py
  pins the refusal as a finding.  On MgSO4 the closed form runs, and the
  lesson is the gap: about 58 % rejection against the solved pore's 99.98 %.

  WHAT TO LOOK AT.  The two MgSO4 R_obs, and the [DSPM-DE] lines: the node
  count, the Newton iterations, the residual, the block-tridiagonal
  structure VERIFIED on the first solve, and the pore summary per unit
  (flux constancy, zero current and electroneutrality, each measured on the
  answer).

  WHAT THIS CASE DOES NOT CLAIM.  Nothing in it is validated against any
  measurement.  The code-to-code comparison with NanoFiltran is
  tutorials/props/membrane/nanofiltran01_dspmde_reference; the grid, the
  residuals and the analytic limit are held by
  bin/curate/check_pore_solver.py.  Shared by all three units: the Davies
  activity at the feed face, an ideal permeate, van't Hoff osmotic
  pressure.

  Data: as membrane10_dspmde_divalent -- the salts carry their ion
  decomposition, the membrane its poreModel{} tier, the ions their radius
  and D0 from the species records.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        NF_NaCl_pore;
        type        spiralWoundModule;
        in          feed_NaCl_pore;
        outputs     ( ret_NaCl_pore  perm_NaCl_pore );
        operation
        {
            membrane         NF270_dspmde;
            transport        DSPM-DE;
            transportParameters
            {
                poreSolver { method finiteDifference;  nodes 101; }
            }
            area             5.0;
            length           1.0;
            P_permeate       1.0 bar;
            k_film           5.0e-5;
            dP_feed_total    1.0 bar;
            nNodes           20;
        }
    }
    {
        name        NF_MgSO4_closedForm;
        type        spiralWoundModule;
        in          feed_MgSO4_closedForm;
        outputs     ( ret_MgSO4_closedForm  perm_MgSO4_closedForm );
        operation
        {
            membrane         NF270_dspmde;
            transport        DSPM-DE;
            transportParameters
            {
                poreSolver { method closedForm; }
            }
            area             5.0;
            length           1.0;
            P_permeate       1.0 bar;
            k_film           5.0e-5;
            dP_feed_total    1.0 bar;
            nNodes           20;
        }
    }
    {
        name        NF_MgSO4_pore;
        type        spiralWoundModule;
        in          feed_MgSO4_pore;
        outputs     ( ret_MgSO4_pore  perm_MgSO4_pore );
        operation
        {
            membrane         NF270_dspmde;
            transport        DSPM-DE;
            transportParameters
            {
                poreSolver { method finiteDifference;  nodes 101; }
            }
            area             5.0;
            length           1.0;
            P_permeate       1.0 bar;
            k_film           5.0e-5;
            dP_feed_total    1.0 bar;
            nNodes           20;
        }
    }
);
